     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Acetaminophen 5000 mg three times daily delivers 15 g/day. That's a hepatotoxic dose for a 70 kg adult, and it's well beyond what's used in any standard regimen. Normal liver function doesn't make it safe. Because the order system may not have a hard stop, I don't want to be the one to put it in.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the safe range.** For example, 1000 mg PO three times daily (3 g/day), or 650 mg PO four times daily (2.6 g/day). The usual maximum is 4 g/day.\n- **Help you check the intent.** If this came from a protocol, a verbal order, or a transcription, it may be a units or decimal error, such as 500 mg.\n- **Involve pharmacy or your attending.** If there's a clinical reason for a nonstandard regimen, they can review it and place it through the proper override process.\n\nTell me which dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
